Subject: [PATCH] SG2000 display: LT8912B lifecycle and DISPPLL/DSI source clocks

drm/bridge: lt8912b
- Power and initialize the receiver in pre_enable, after the DSI host has
  prepared LP-11, instead of at attach; latch timing in enable after the
  host streams; reset the receiver in disable and drop the supplies in
  post_disable. The callbacks are void, so results go to a shared status
  (include/drm/bridge/lt8912b.h) the host binds.
- Without a reset GPIO (the badge's RESET_N is an RC power-on reset) stop
  the receiver through main register 0x03.
- Drop the LVDS setup and the independent PM resume, which would release
  reset and start video without the host. Detach from the host before the
  bridge is removed.

clk: sophgo
- SG2000 TRM v1.0 (sophgo/sophgo-doc 370d81b365ed528dc8f5dc91f63ed445e1142d4d,
  pll_g2 and pll_g6 register tables): lock bits are 16..20 (G2) and 16..18
  (G6); the driver polled the updating bits 0..4.
- DISPPLL reports rate 0 while powered down, unlocked or updating, uncached,
  so a consumer can observe lock after enabling it.
- Expose the DSI PHY synthesizer source gate (pll_g2_ssc_syn_ctrl bit 1) as
  clk_dsi_synth_src, binding id 162, without retuning MIPIMPLL.

Prepared with Claude and Codex assistance.

